# ── Chat Assistant (portfolio AI) ───────────────────────────────
# The chat route uses the OpenAI SDK, so any OpenAI-compatible
# provider works. Pick ONE option below, then:
#   1. Copy this file to .env
#   2. Fill in the values for your chosen option
#   3. Restart the dev server (and set the same vars on your host
#      when deployed)

# ── Option A: OpenAI (paid, key starts with "sk-") ──────────────
# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
# Prepaid credits required, minimum $5. gpt-4o-mini is very cheap
# (~$0.0002 per short conversation).
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key-here
# CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ── Option B: Google Gemini (free tier, no credit card) ─────────
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Free tier: Gemini Flash models with daily request limits.
# Model names change over time; if a model is retired for your key, the
# API error message suggests the current replacement.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
# CHAT_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# ── Option C: Groq (free tier, very fast) ───────────────────────
# https://console.groq.com/keys
# Free tier with daily limits. Groq does not retain inference data
# by default.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
# CHAT_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# ── Option D: OpenRouter (free models, one key) ─────────────────
# https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Free models end with ":free"; rotate over time, check
# https://openrouter.ai/models?max_price=0
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openrouter-api-key
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# CHAT_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct:free

# Notes:
# - Free tiers may log or train on request data. Fine for a public
#   portfolio FAQ bot; do not send sensitive information.
# - Never commit .env to git (already in .gitignore).
# - Secrets are declared in astro.config.mjs (env.schema) and read at
#   runtime: values never end up inside dist/, and variables set on the
#   hosting platform always take effect.
# - Local check of the production build:
#   npm run build
#   $env:PORT=4322; node dist/server/entry.mjs   (then open :4322)
